            <ArticleTitle>Cardiac surgery in patients on antiplatelet and antithrombotic agents.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>66-72</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The widespread application of antithrombotic agents carries significant potential for inducing excessive peri-operative hemorrhage during cardiac surgery. Specific surgical and medical strategies can be employed to attenuate this bleeding. These antithrombotic agents and anti-hemorrhagic measures will be reviewed in depth.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
